/**
 * B6-kol-daily-sync F006 · BL-012 crawler-team adapter STUB.
 *
 * NOT WIRED. This file ends in `.ts.todo` on purpose — TypeScript and
 * the dispatcher both ignore it. It exists to (a) prove the
 * KolSyncAdapter contract maps cleanly onto the schema described in
 * docs/product/kol-crawler-team-handoff-v1.md §3-§4, and (b) keep the
 * 6-月 接入路径 below visible at the place a future engineer will
 * actually open.
 *
 * Promote this to `crawler-team.ts` by following §"6 月接入步骤" at
 * the bottom of this file. Expected effort: ~1 day end-to-end.
 *
 * --- Contract mapping (handoff-v1 §3 → KolSyncAdapter) ---
 *
 *   handoff §3.1 (10 core fields)            RawKolData (types.ts)
 *   ─────────────────────────────────────    ───────────────────────────
 *   externalId (string)                      externalId
 *   platform (enum)                          platform
 *   handle (string)                          handle
 *   displayName (string)                     displayName
 *   url (string)                             — derived in import.ts
 *                                              from platform + handle
 *   avatarUrl (string|null)                  thumbnailUrl
 *   countryCode (ISO-2)                      country
 *   followerCount (int)                      subscriberCount
 *   categories (string[])                    topicCategories
 *                                              (passes through
 *                                              import.ts deriveCategories)
 *   isGaming (bool)                          — pre-filtered upstream
 *                                              by the crawler team
 *
 *   handoff §3.2 (15-dim extension fields)
 *   ─────────────────────────────────────
 *   language (ISO-639-1)                     language
 *   engagementRate (decimal)                 raw.engagementRate
 *   avgViews (int)                           raw.avgViews
 *   uploadsPerMonth (int)                    raw.uploadsPerMonth
 *   lastUploadAt (ISO 8601)                  lastUploadAt
 *   monetizationStatus (enum)                raw.monetizationStatus
 *   brandSafetyRating (enum)                 brandSafetyRating
 *   knownBrandCollabs (string[])             raw.knownBrandCollabs
 *   audienceAgeDist (json)                   raw.audienceAgeDist
 *   audienceGeoDist (json)                   raw.audienceGeoDist
 *   audienceGenderDist (json)                raw.audienceGenderDist
 *   engagementAuthenticity (int 0-100)       raw.engagementAuthenticity
 *   bio (text)                               description
 *   tags (string[])                          raw.tags
 *   email (string|null)                      raw.email
 *
 *   handoff §3.5 (metadata)                  RawKolData
 *   ─────────────────────────────────────    ───────────────────────────
 *   dataQuality                              raw.dataQuality
 *   fieldSources                             raw.fieldSources
 *   lastCrawledAt (ISO 8601)                 scrapedAt
 *   crawlerVersion                           raw.crawlerVersion
 *
 *   --- API mapping (handoff §4 → KolSyncAdapter methods) ---
 *
 *   discover()        →  GET /v1/kols?platform=youtube&country_code=…
 *                                       &min_followers=…&categories=…
 *                                       &cursor=…&limit=…
 *                        (walk pages until next_cursor === null)
 *
 *   refresh(ids)      →  GET /v1/kols/:externalId   per id
 *                        (handoff §4.4; the crawler team has flagged
 *                        a future bulk endpoint POST /v1/kols/lookup
 *                        in §10 — promote when shipped)
 *
 *   healthCheck()     →  GET /v1/kols?limit=1
 *                        (no dedicated probe endpoint; a 200 with at
 *                        least one item proves auth + freshness +
 *                        non-empty corpus)
 *
 * The 30s/2min/5min retry schedule from F004 already wraps every
 * adapter call at the dispatcher level — this adapter MUST stay
 * stateless and surface 5xx / 429 as thrown errors so withRetry
 * picks them up. 429 with Retry-After (handoff §4.6) is a reason to
 * reconsider whether the schedule should respect that header — log
 * the value for now, no special-casing.
 */

